function teachingFor(n){const map={E01:'Part A helps cover hospital care. Part B helps cover medical care. Together, Parts A and B are Original Medicare. What would help next?',E02:'Part D covers prescription drugs. With Original Medicare it is a separate plan; most Medicare Advantage plans include it. What would help next?',E03:'Original Medicare is Parts A and B, with optional separate Part D and Medigap. Medicare Advantage (Part C) is another way to get A and B and usually includes Part D. Medigap does not pair with Advantage. What would help next?',E04:'A premium is the amount paid each month. Deductibles, copays and coinsurance are costs when getting care. Compare total costs and what is covered, not just premiums. What would help next?',A03:'Medicare is federal health insurance that helps pay for health care. We can explain only what you need.',C00:'Part A helps cover hospital care. Part B helps cover medical care. Together they are Original Medicare.',C03:'Tell us what is in place now. An insurance name alone does not verify its benefits.',O00:'Original Medicare is Parts A and B. Choose a coverage category, then how you want to explore it.',N00:'Part D is prescription drug coverage. A medicine name alone does not establish coverage or cost.',N03:'Routine dental, vision and hearing benefits need a separate check.',N04:'Monthly premiums and costs when getting care are different. Choose what matters to you.',N05:'If priorities conflict, this helps identify what you want to check first.',J03:'Employment and health coverage can end in different months. Keep the dates separate.',O11:'Medigap helps with certain Original Medicare costs. It does not work with Medicare Advantage.'};if(['A01','A02','L01'].includes(n.id))return '';return map[n.id]||n.why||'';}
